       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg PO three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day). A 2,000 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. Even with normal liver function, this carries a serious risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that might match what you intended:\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf 2000 mg three times daily is intentional, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the rationale and I can enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me which of the doses above you'd like, or give me a different one, and I'll enter it right away."
